# The default V8 heap OOMs when building this app on a small VM (4.4 GB, e.g. the Hermes VM / the
# Steam Deck): `vite build` dies with v8::FatalProcessOutOfMemory. Setting it here rather than in the
# `build` script keeps `npm run build` working bare — and cross-platform, since `NODE_OPTIONS=... vite
# build` in package.json would not run under cmd.exe. npm applies `node-options` to every lifecycle
# script (build, test, check), which is what we want: a max, not a reservation.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=2600
